AND
CITY OF CHEYENNE TRANSIT PROGRAM
1.
Parties.The parties to this Agreement are Wyoming Department of Health, Aging
Division (Agency), whose address is:2300 Capitol Avenue, 4th Floor, Cheyenne,
Wyoming82002, and City of Cheyenne Transit Program(Sub recipient), whose addressis:
322West Lincolnway, Cheyenne, Wyoming,82001.
2.
Purpose of Agreement.The purpose of this Agreement is to set forth the terms and
conditions by which the Sub recipient shall provide Title II-B Support Services of the
Older Americans Act of1965, as amended in 2020, to eligible individuals in the Agreement
service area of Laramie County, Wyoming, as more specifically defined in Grant
Application, which is incorporated into this Agreement by this reference.The purpose of
the TitleIII programs is to provide services to vulnerable adults in order to promote
independence, living with dignity, and maintenance of their health and fitness.
3.
Term of Agreement.This Agreement is effective when all parties have executed it
(Effective Date).The term of this Agreement is from October 1,2024, or the Effective
Date, whichever is later, through November 15,2025.All services shall be completed
during this term.The Period of Performance for Grant activities under this Agreement is
from October 1,2024, through September 30,2025.Sub recipient must utilize all funds
associated with this Agreement during the Period of Performance.
4.
Payment.
A.
The Agency agrees to pay the Sub recipient for the services described in Section5
below, the services describedin Attachment A, Statement of Work, whichis
attached to and incorporated into this Agreement by this reference, and the services
described in Grant Application, which is incorporated into this Agreement by this
reference, in accordance with payment limits based on the funding source. The
payment limits for Title II funds are established as follows:
Total payment under this Agreement shall not exceed sixty-two thousand
six hundred twenty dollars ($62,620.00).
(i)
The payment of Title II Funds is subject to the following conditions:
a.The maximum amount of federal funds provided under CFDA#93.044
TitleIHI-BSupportive Services shall not exceed fifty-eight thousand
three hundred seventy-five dollars ($58,375.00).
b.Themaximum amount of state matching funds provided for Title III-B
Supportive Services shall not exceed four thousand twohundred forty-
five dollars ($4,245.00).
